{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790960682,"nonce":"A3i0kcPxyZ+fYOoLCPPfp6BzD5M=","title":"a wasm program cannot ask its host to start a browser agent","message":"xgpu and xwindow serve a browser API from an agent on the page: the program asks its host to start one by name with an address in shared memory, and the host imports `\u003cname\u003e.mjs` beside the program and calls its `start({ memory, address, canvas })`. Caribou does this through `host::agent`, Ash through `ash_host_agent(name, len, address)`. Rayzor has no equivalent, so neither library's web backend can run in a Rayzor program; rayzor-gpu's browser path is a separate wasm-bindgen API instead.\n\nThe hook belongs in Rayzor's wasm harness (src/wasm_cmd.rs) and its plugin carriers, with shared memory where `crossOriginIsolated` allows it. See xgpu's README, \"Wasm host contract\".","files":null}]}